're showing good pressure  reproducibility on both the binary and  the quaternary pumps  we get excellent retention time  stability  good peak shape and we maintain  separation of the linear and branched  isomers  some robustness data for the online sbe  so this chart shows both pfos and pifoa  with their  isotopically labeled analogs the green  boxes show the calibrators  and then s3 and s4 are repeated  injections of these alternating samples  and you can see that even you know for a  very long  alter many alternating runs that they  maintain really good  area counts with the one exception um is  that there does to  appear to be a saturated peak in sample  s3  and that really kind of highlights an uh  you know an additional benefit  of the online system is if you have some  kind of saturation like that  instead of having to actually dilute the  sample you can just inject less  all the injection volumes that for these  samples that you see  is 475 microliters  and that's also another benefit is if  you're doing an offline system you have  to extract 250 milliliters  here you only need 475 microliters  and that is essentially that whole mass  is essentially injected onto your  analytical  columns you can get some really great  sensitivity  and here i'm showing the linearity now  all the results that i've presented so  far for this off  online spe system are on the 6470  and with this injection volume we get  really great  sensitivity down to 0.1 nanogram per  liter for pfoa  and one nanogram per liter for pfos so  far today i've only really been talking  about the targeted workflow  and as the title indicated i'm going to  talk a little bit now about untargeted  screening  which you would typically do with a  high-res mass spec instrument  and the one i'll highlight for this  application is the 6546  it's the most recent addition to our  qtof portfolio  and it's a lot like the 6545 except for  it has a lot more muscle  it allows the acquisition of data in  high resolution and extended dynamic  range  it also has a higher resolution than any  of our previous trip or qtof models  at 108 at 118 mass over charge that  provides over 30 000 in resolution  it also includes some new acquisition  features such as  quadrupole resolved all ions and it does  have the capillary gate valve  as i discussed for the triple quads  and best of all it has the same  sensitivity isotope fidelity and  robustness that was  made the 6545 so popular  when using high reso high resolution  mass spec really allows you to do  screening for a large number of  compounds quickly  you can start by building a personal  compound database library  this can include as little as just an  accurate mass or as much as collision  spectra and retention  time we do have libraries available for  purchase while one for  pfast is not yet available we do have a  water contaminated database that does  include some pfast compounds  quickly screening your data set can  allow you to tentatively  identify emerging pfas once you do  further experiments  to fully just elucidate the structure  that spectra and retention time data can  be added to the pcdl  another benefit of high-res mass spec  data  is that when you run your sample you  collect a full spectral scan for that  whole sample  which allows you to re-review historical  samples once you identify new compounds  and that is really not possible with  triple quad data  this particular slide illustrates a pdf  pcdl scanning a wastewater sample and  the identification of 62fts throughout  the water treatment process  to complement the suspect screening  there is a true non-targeted analysis  this involves identifying new pfas  compounds  and to do this you really need structure  elucidation tools such as targeted msms  and software which will allow you to  create fragments and then software tools  that help you identify those fragments  and rebuild a structure that they come  from  and one of those software trolls that we  offer is the molecular structure  correlator  once you fully identify these compounds  you can add them to your pcdl  and your rescan your historical data  during this presentation i have  discussed kind of two approaches for  characterizing pfas in the environment  and they are complementary we have the  complete workflow available from  analyzing known knowns to identifying  unknown and emerging pfas compounds i  hope the information presented has been  useful and would be happy to answer any  questions via email  and of course i'd like to acknowledge  all my collaborators and  colleagues i didn't generate much of the  data i presented here myself so of  course i would like to give credit  where credit is due so thanks thanks to  all of them  and of course thank you to you for your  attention
 

